# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/bin/
/dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Save data. Never commit any of this.
#
# A KH3 save embeds the owner's SteamID64 and their entire playthrough. Tests
# and CI build synthetic saves instead (tools/genfixture), so nothing here
# is ever needed by the build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/saves/
KHIII_*.bin
*.bak.*
*.zip

# `kh3save dump -with-account` writes the SteamID64 into its JSON, and a dump
# is exactly the kind of file that gets left in a working tree. Ignore the
# extension, then un-ignore the ones that genuinely belong to the repo by name.
*.json
!testdata/golden.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerable working directories
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream KingdomSaveEditor clone. tools/gen_tables.py re-clones it at a
# pinned commit, so it never needs to be committed.
# (gitignore has no trailing-comment syntax, so a comment on the pattern line
# becomes part of the pattern and silently matches nothing.)
/refs/
/work/
/out/
/extracted/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python (only tools/gen_tables.py remains, and it is build-time codegen)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Assistant / agent scratch
#
# Working notes and local agent config. These often carry machine paths,
# internal hostnames and half-formed reasoning that has no business in a
# public repo, so they are excluded by default rather than case by case.
# If a project-level instruction file is ever meant to ship, un-ignore it
# deliberately with a negation rather than deleting these lines.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/
.claudeignore
AGENTS.md
.cursor/
.cursorrules
.aider*
.continue/
.windsurfrules
.opencode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# compose reads this automatically, and the natural thing to put in it is the
# path to your save folder, which names your account.
.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# The Python reference implementation was removed once the Go tool reached
# parity; its output is frozen in testdata/golden.json. Kept ignored so a local
# copy never lands in a commit.
/reference/
